  "method": {
    "root_existence": "For each admitted latitude and polar leg, the outer edge has normalized Mino time below m times the half-period for all m at or above the recorded cutoff. The time diverges inward. The parent strict residual slope bound leaves one continuous radial root for every stationary inverse radius.",
    "azimuth": "At a latitude root, azimuth is m times the sum of half-period polar azimuth and turning drag, plus two partial polar integrals and the finite spin remainder. Differentiate along the implicit latitude root; the transverse correction is bounded by a decreasing quadratic times (19/64)^m. This proves strict tangential monotonicity throughout the chart.",
    "geometry": "The number of unwrapped azimuth roots modulo 2*pi is at most 1+wrap_count_slope*m on each of the two polar legs. The determinant multiplies source polar velocity, the latitude residual slope, tangential azimuth slope and the original film Jacobian. The latter is transformed from h to log(s) using h=-s\u00b2. The inverse determinant is bounded by inverse_determinant_coefficient*s\u00b2/m.",
    "flux": "Use the exact represented catalogue intensities, positive Gaussian majorant, Rayleigh-Jeans Planck upper bound, absolute CIE matrix row bound and reduced normalizer floor. The conservative geometric sum covers all later m and both polar legs. The exponent is kept separate until multiplying by the flux envelope."
  },
